<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kristang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kristang people, Portuguese Eurasians of Malacca</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kristang are a Eurasian community of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> in Malaysia and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, descended from Portuguese settlers of the 16th and 17th centuries who married local women. They are mostly Roman Catholic and speak, or once spoke, Papia Kristang, a Portuguese-based <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">creole</a>. A settlement founded for them in Malacca in the 1930s, the Portuguese Settlement, remains the centre of their community.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kristang.jpg" alt="Kristang" width="320" height="280" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Victor pogadaev at Russian Wikipedia · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kristangi_Malacca.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
